dialect protocol
protocol stdio.las.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.las
start document
framing record

# Ticket 26/08/10/ARTIFACT-SYSTEM-OVERHAUL-REAL-CODECS-RUNTIME-REUSE-EVOLUTION: real byte layout
# matching engine::{encode_las, decode_las} (../../../../⚙️engine/🦀️component.rs's `off`/
# `vlr_off` modules) EXACTLY -- replacing the placeholder ABNF-flavored text the previous (F2)
# wave left here (that file used `%x`/single-quoted literals/`SP`/`NL`/bare `2OCTET` productions
# entirely outside this framework's REAL `.protocol.semio` dialect -- `dialect protocol\nprotocol
# <id>\nversion <n>\nschema <id>\nstart <block>\nframing ...`, `field <name> <prim>` inside a
# `header fixed N` block, per the ticket's own grammar-recipe doc §2). LAS 1.0's public header
# block is FIXED 227 bytes at named byte offsets -- genuinely, field-by-field protocol-walkable.
# `framing record` (not `framing magic`) is used deliberately: `Framing::Magic` ALWAYS consumes
# exactly 8 bytes at position 0 (confirmed by direct read of `walk_protocol`'s `Framing::Magic`
# arm, `🗣️dsl/📖️grammar/🦀️component.rs`), but LAS's real signature is only 4 bytes ("LASF") --
# too short for that framing mode. The signature is instead modeled as the header's own first
# field (`magic fixed 4`, an honest real 4-byte span; content-equality against literal "LASF" is a
# Rust-side concern, same as every other unvalidated `fixed`/`bytes` span in this dialect, not
# something the protocol walker checks).
#
# What follows the header (Variable Length Records, whose repeat COUNT comes from an
# earlier-decoded header field rather than a per-iteration tag/sentinel byte, then point records,
# whose FIXED-WIDTH shape is chosen ONCE by an earlier header field rather than re-declared per
# iteration) hits the `protocol-array-of-records` gap this program's other binary-native pilots
# (zip's `entries`, this artifact's own diff/mutations facets) already hit and filed --
# `Block::Repeat`'s `arms` are tag-dispatched per iteration, and `Prim::Array` only repeats one
# FIXED-WIDTH scalar; neither can express "repeat N times, N from an earlier field, each iteration
# a multi-field record" (VLRs), nor "an earlier field selects which of several fixed record shapes
# every following iteration uses" (point records, format 0-3). The real Rust `decode_las`/
# `encode_las` (this file's whole point) walk this genuinely, field-by-field, VLR-by-VLR,
# point-by-point, independently round-trip tested (`⚙️engine/🦀️component.rs`'s 11 tests) -- this
# protocol description honestly bounds only what it can field-by-field walk: the real fixed
# header, then one opaque trailing chain for the VLR list + point list combined.

header fixed 227
field magic fixed 4
field file_source_id fixed 2
field global_encoding fixed 2
field project_id_guid fixed 16
field version_major u8
field version_minor u8
field system_identifier fixed 32
field generating_software fixed 32
field creation_day_of_year u16
field creation_year u16
field header_size u16
field offset_to_point_data u32
field number_of_vlrs u32
field point_data_format_id u8
field point_data_record_length u16
field number_of_point_records u32
field points_by_return_1 u32
field points_by_return_2 u32
field points_by_return_3 u32
field points_by_return_4 u32
field points_by_return_5 u32
field x_scale f64
field y_scale f64
field z_scale f64
field x_offset f64
field y_offset f64
field z_offset f64
field max_x f64
field min_x f64
field max_y f64
field min_y f64
field max_z f64
field min_z f64

chain payload bytes
